---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/privacy.css';

const lastUpdated = 'August 3, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Important limitations and responsible-use guidance for Security Cards."
  analytics={{ pageType: 'disclaimer' }}
>
  <div class="page-wrapper legal">
    <section class="hero">
      <span class="hero-eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Disclaimer</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        Security Cards provides practical, version-specific guidance to support secure software
        development. It does not replace professional judgment, testing, or a security review of
        your particular system.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </section>

    <aside class="legal-notice" aria-labelledby="responsible-use-title">
      <h2 class="legal-notice-title" id="responsible-use-title">Use the cards as guidance</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">
        We review cards before publication, but review cannot guarantee that every card is complete,
        error-free, or suitable for every project. Verify guidance against the referenced library
        version, official documentation, your threat model, and your own tests before relying on it.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Informational purpose</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">
        The cards and all related content are provided for general informational and educational
        purposes. They are not legal, compliance, audit, or professional security advice, and using
        them does not create a professional, advisory, or fiduciary relationship with RewareLabs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2 class="legal-h2">No guarantee of accuracy or completeness</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">
        Security practices, libraries, and their documentation change over time. Although we make
        reasonable efforts to review and maintain the cards, the content may contain mistakes,
        omissions, outdated information, or examples that do not apply to your environment. We do
        not warrant that the content is accurate, complete, current, secure, or fit for a particular
        purpose.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Use of artificial intelligence</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">
        We use generative artificial intelligence tools to assist with researching, drafting, and
        refining Security Cards. This means that some card content is AI-generated or
        AI-assisted. In the interest of transparency, including the principles reflected in the EU
        AI Act, we disclose that use here.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-p">
        We review cards before publication, but human review does not eliminate the possibility of
        AI-related errors, omissions, bias, fabricated information, or outdated guidance. AI output
        is not treated as an authoritative source. You should verify each card against the cited
        sources, official library documentation, and the requirements of your own system.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Your responsibility</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">
        You are responsible for evaluating whether a card applies to your software and for the
        design, implementation, testing, deployment, and operation of your systems. Always review
        changes in context, use appropriate automated and manual security testing, and obtain
        qualified professional advice where the risk or applicable law requires it.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-p">
        A card does not guarantee that software is secure or free from vulnerabilities, and the
        absence of a topic from a card should not be understood as evidence that no risk exists.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Third-party software and links</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">
        Security Cards discusses and links to third-party libraries, repositories, and
        documentation. Those projects are controlled by their respective owners. RewareLabs does
        not endorse or control their content, availability, security, licensing, or future changes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">
        To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Security Cards and its content are
        provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind, whether express or
        implied. RewareLabs and its contributors will not be liable for any loss, damage, claim, or
        expense arising from or related to your use of, inability to use, or reliance on the cards
        or related content.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-p">
        Nothing in this disclaimer excludes or limits liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or
        limited.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
      <h2 class="legal-h2">Changes</h2>
      <p class="legal-p">
        We may revise the cards or this disclaimer as the project evolves. The date above identifies
        the latest published version of this page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
